 "mc_note": "ROBUST-A: 3 breaches in 600 unseen trips (all shallow, cold aged packs on the descent) and 87 % of ORACLE's regen. The industry-style fixed 10 mV margin keeps all the energy but breaches on 14 % of trips; SoC-only margins (ROBUST, LEANHIGH) breach on a third, because on the graphite plateau a SoC shift barely moves the plating limit. kA = 3 chosen on 600 separate training trips.",
 "rw_note": "ROBUST-A's price: about ₹300-430 a year for a private car and ₹3,400 for a ride-hailing car. In return it removes almost every plating trip, of which SOP has 150-180 a year for a private car and about 4,500 for a ride-hailing car.",
 "conclusions": [
  [
   "Asymmetry",
   "Overestimate loses regen (+2 % → 10 %, +5 % → 87 % from 95 % SoC); underestimate eats a 4-9 mV plating margin."
  ],
  [
   "Two bands",
   "Accuracy matters near full and at the graphite step (65-75 % SoC); below 60 %, ±10 % is harmless."
  ],
  [
   "The pack",
   "With a perfect SoC, cell spread alone plates the weakest cell in nearly every pack; kinetics and temperature spread dominate."
  ],
  [
   "ROBUST-A",
   "0.5 % of unseen trips breached (95 % CI 0.2-1.5 %) vs 14-45 % for the alternatives; keeps 87 % of the oracle's regen."
  ],
  [
   "In India",
   "About ₹300-430 a year for a private car, ₹3,400 for a ride-hailing car, to avoid hundreds to thousands of plating trips."
  ]
 ]
